REVIEW-FIX — the IMPORTANT was a genuine operator trap: two comments in scrape.go made incompatible claims, one selling MaxConfigurableBytes as a container-safety property while the other correctly said peak is the body cap times the parser expansion factor. An operator hitting ErrBodyTooLarge would read 16 MiB as headroom, raise the cap against a 64Mi limit and OOM the pod, taking the heartbeat down with the resource metrics. The ceiling is now documented as a sanity bound on operator input and nothing more, and values.yaml plus the README env row both say raising the cap is only safe together with resources.limits.memory and agent.goMemLimit. Also taken: a doc comment on the caller-assigned Agent.Metrics field, and a README note that the NetworkPolicy guard is breaking for an existing release running enabled=true with the default empty from.
