LOG CORRECTION — the fix-round-8 entry above was written with a backticked word that the shell evaluated before the append, dropping "with" from the sentence. Restored; no other line was affected.
REVIEW ROUND 8 (five aspects over the round-8 delta) — 0 CRITICAL, 16 IMPORTANT, 21 SUGGESTION. Two security gaps and four real defects, several of them mine from round 8.
FIX-ROUND-9 SECURITY — the credential refusal ran only in the binary, so by the time it fired the ConfigMap was already applied to the cluster and stored in the Helm release: detection after the write, while the README read as prevention. Both URLs are now refused at RENDER time in validateValues, so helm install aborts before anything reaches etcd, and the startup check stays as defence in depth. Second gap: validateScrapeURL was reached only in the exposition and auto modes although configmap.yaml writes the key in all four, so a credential in an unused scrape URL was stored in clear text with no warning; it is now checked whenever the value is set, at render time and in requiredConfig.
FIX-ROUND-9 BUGS — sprig's toString renders an absent value as "<nil>", not "", so --set agent.goMemLimit=null failed the render naming a value the operator never set; reproduced, then fixed with a kind check. A mistyped agent.mode rendered neither workload and reported success, which is the same silent no-op class the chart already refuses elsewhere; now rejected. rateCounters called Observe with nothing on a tick where no role was rateable, wiping every counter predecessor and costing a service a SECOND tick of CPU once the family returned — the exact outcome the function's own doc comment refuses for the attribution case; mutation-verified. cronjob.yaml still carried the bare-truthiness guard round 8 removed elsewhere; all three sites now derive from one nil-safe helper.
FIX-ROUND-9 CI — the gate asserted key NAMES only, so an API key accidentally rendered into the ConfigMap would have passed; assertions are now scoped to the ConfigMap document, check values for the URL and the interval suffix, and fail if the API key appears there at all. The key list is derived from the template that owns it rather than retyped. Each shape declares what it proves with an "# expect:" marker instead of the workflow grepping the values file's source text, and metrics-on and metrics-off now assert what actually differs (METRICS_ENABLED, the container port, the Service) rather than an identical set. Cronjob shapes assert --once, whose loss would turn a scheduled one-shot into a never-terminating Job. Added shapes for a null and an unquoted-integer goMemLimit and for podAnnotations; added refusals for 0, 00, -1MiB, a mistyped mode, and credentials in either URL including in metrics-server mode.
FIX-ROUND-9 SELF-CAUGHT — the new content assertion immediately failed on my own new shape: an unquoted 58720256 in a values FILE is parsed as a float and toString renders 5.8720256e+07. The helper now formats a float back to a plain integer, so both the --set and the values-file paths work.
FIX-ROUND-9 NOT REPRODUCED — the bugs reviewer held at 80 percent confidence that the negative GOMEMLIMIT assertion, an A && B list under set -euo pipefail, would abort the step on its correct outcome. I extracted the exact step from the workflow with a YAML loader and ran it: exit 0. Bash exempts the left operand of && from errexit, inside an if/else branch as well. The claim is withdrawn, and the step was rewritten in the explicit if/then form anyway, because no reader should have to reason about errexit exemptions to trust a gate.
FIX-ROUND-9 EVIDENCE CORRECTION — my round-8 packet claimed five negative goMemLimit values were exercised; the committed workflow encoded three, and the two missing ones included the bare 0 that round 8 existed to fix. The reviewers were right to call that out. All six are now in the workflow, so the claim and the gate agree.
FIX-ROUND-9 TESTS — the round-8 relocation script had cut one doc comment in half across two files, matching the continuation's leading word to an unrelated method; restored, and a sweep of every doc block in the tree found no second instance. Added: requiredConfig with nine cases plus a per-mode scrape-URL case; envDuration's non-positive fallback; the two Debug diagnostics, which were the only consumer of Selection.Excluded and were invisible because every test logger sat at Warn; the Rater keeping state across a tick with no rateable role. The candidate table now builds its counter cases as counters and asserts Kind and Rateable, instead of naming them counters and passing gauges. Both transport-error tests now use a refusing RoundTripper rather than a just-closed ephemeral port and the platform's syscall wording.
FIX-ROUND-9 CONVENTIONS — reporter_test.go and k8s_test.go split out, so every source file in internal/agent has its own test file; the three exposition helpers moved beside their types; every top-level declaration separated by a blank line; the _helpers.tpl comment now says what the chart does (deployment and cronjob include the validator before their mode guard, so one reachable include covers every render) instead of claiming a per-template convention it does not follow; internal/scrape no longer names the backend wire keys it does not own; ValidateAPIURL moved next to the Reporter it validates for; the README lets the config table own the URL rule and links to it from the other two places; the ci/ shapes carry a README instead of repeating the same header seven times, and it names what is still uncovered.
